--- dependent -- indexed families and dependent structure (ADR-0120 Phase 4;
--- research/PAPER.md section 5).
---
--- ## Vocabulary
---
--- Types are objects and arrows are morphisms; dependent structure is
--- family structure over an object -- no separate type-theoretic
--- subsystem. The typecheck model recognizes the surface formers as
--- ordinary calls in type-expression position:
---
---   Family(A)           -- the type of A-indexed families (A ~~ Type)
---   Pi(A, x ~> B)       -- dependent function type Pi (x:A), B(x)
---   Sigma(A, x ~> B)    -- dependent pair type Sigma (x:A), B(x)
---   Forall(K, x ~> B)   -- type-level quantification Forall (x:K), B(x)
---   Type / Universe / Type0 -- the universe (level 0)
---
--- `data Name(i...) :: Ctor | ...` declares an inductive family: `Name`
--- binds a `type.family` and each constructor a `type.ctor_sig` that is
--- freshly instantiated per use -- a `type.function` chain over the
--- constructor domains ending in a `type.family_app` at the declared
--- result indices. A declared family shadows the builtin spelling, so
--- `data Nat :: Zero | Succ(pred : Nat)` makes `Nat` the inductive
--- family and `Succ(Zero)` checks while `Succ(3)` does not.
---
--- ## Index terms compute
---
--- Family indices are normalized before unification: closed arithmetic
--- evaluates (`Vec(1 + 1)` is `Vec(2)`), commutative operands
--- canonicalize (`1 + n` ≡ `n + 1`), the ring identities apply
--- (`n + 0`, `n * 1`, `n - 0`, `n / 1`, `n * 0`), nested literal bins
--- merge (`(n - 1) + 1` ≡ `n`), and reflexive comparisons fold
--- (`n == n` ≡ `true`). Symbolic indices that stay unequal do not unify
--- -- `Vec(n)` and `Vec(n + 1)` differ -- and `Bin`-vs-literal
--- unification solves only the linear fragment (`X + c = t`, `X - c = t`,
--- `X * c = t`, and mirrors).
---
--- ## Reindexing is composition
---
--- For `f : A ~> B` and `P : Family(B)` the pullback family `f* P` on `A`
--- is ordinary composition `f >>> P` -- there is no reindexing primitive.
--- `reindex` is the derived arrow.

export reindex := (f, P) ~> f >>> P

--- ## The adjunction Sigma_f -| f* -| Pi_f
---
--- Dependent sum and product along `f` are the left and right adjoints of
--- pullback `f* = f >>> -`. The unit/counit laws are ordinary 2-cell
--- terms `~[2]~>` (PAPER.md section 4 -- laws are higher morphisms), each
--- bound as an arrow over its participants: the family `P`/`Q`, the
--- reindexing morphism `f`, and the adjoint former `Sigma_f`/`Pi_f`
--- applied along `f`.
---
---   sigma_unit   : Q ~[2]~> f* (Sigma_f Q)     -- unit of Sigma_f -| f*
---   sigma_counit : Sigma_f (f* P) ~[2]~> P     -- counit of Sigma_f -| f*
---   pi_unit      : P ~[2]~> Pi_f (f* P)        -- unit of f* -| Pi_f
---   pi_counit    : f* (Pi_f Q) ~[2]~> Q        -- counit of f* -| Pi_f

export sigma_unit := (Q, f, Sigma_f) ~> Q ~[2]~> (f >>> Sigma_f(Q))
export sigma_counit := (P, f, Sigma_f) ~> Sigma_f((f >>> P)) ~[2]~> P
export pi_unit := (P, f, Pi_f) ~> P ~[2]~> Pi_f((f >>> P))
export pi_counit := (Q, f, Pi_f) ~> (f >>> Pi_f(Q)) ~[2]~> Q

--- ## Scope of the structural fragment
---
--- This is a structural shadow, not full dependent type checking.
--- Index terms DO compute (see "Index terms compute" above) and
--- constructor arguments ARE checked through freshly instantiated
--- `type.ctor_sig` signatures, including dependent domains like
--- `VCons(x : a, xs : Vec(n, a))`. The remaining limitations:
---
---   * strict positivity is checked by the `desugar.data` native
---     rather than the typechecker;
---   * `match` binds constructor-pattern fields against the
---     instantiated constructor domains, but does NOT refine the
---     scrutinee's family index per branch -- writing
---     `match v { VNil: ..., VCons(x, xs): ... }` does not teach the
---     checker that `v : Vec(0, a)` in the first arm. True dependent
---     elimination needs an equality type/proof term (`v ≡ Ctor ...`)
---     to rewrite the index under each arm, machinery the structural
---     shadow deliberately does not carry;
---   * a composite `f >>> P` of dependent operands flattens to
---     `type.function` because no AST body exists to carry a
---     `body_closure` across composition.
